usage: bringup.py [-h] --bit BIT --hwh HWH [--firmware FIRMWARE]
                  [--bit-sha256 BIT_SHA256] [--hwh-sha256 HWH_SHA256]
                  [--firmware-sha256 FIRMWARE_SHA256] (--download |
                  --use-loaded) [--control-ip CONTROL_IP] [--dma-ip DMA_IP]
                  [--lock-path LOCK_PATH] [--modes MODES] [--smoke] [--full]
                  [--benchmark REPETITIONS] [--message-bytes MESSAGE_BYTES]
                  [--ad-bytes AD_BYTES] [--timeout TIMEOUT] --output OUTPUT

Permanent PYNQ 2.7 DMA ABI v2 smoke/full-KAT/benchmark CLI. No hardware is
emulated by this CLI. Offline tests inject an explicitly simulated transport
into run_checks. Firmware hashes identify supplied build artifacts, not
firmware readback (the control ABI has no firmware-digest register).

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --bit BIT
  --hwh HWH
  --firmware FIRMWARE   CPU build artifact; required for modes 1/2/3
  --bit-sha256 BIT_SHA256
  --hwh-sha256 HWH_SHA256
  --firmware-sha256 FIRMWARE_SHA256
  --download
  --use-loaded
  --control-ip CONTROL_IP
  --dma-ip DMA_IP
  --lock-path LOCK_PATH
  --modes MODES         auto or comma-separated 1,2,3,4
  --smoke
  --full
  --benchmark REPETITIONS
  --message-bytes MESSAGE_BYTES
  --ad-bytes AD_BYTES
  --timeout TIMEOUT
  --output OUTPUT
